{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-job-006",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 6,
  "title": "Job 6",
  "display_title": "Job 6",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "job",
  "book": "Job",
  "bookName": "Job",
  "bookOrder": 18,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 6,
  "sortOrder": 18006,
  "verseCount": 30,
  "aliases": [
    "Job"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:6:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "But Job answered and said,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 6:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:6:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:6:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Oh that my grief were throughly weighed, and my calamity laid in the balances together!",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 6:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:6:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:6:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "For now it would be heavier than the sand of the sea: therefore my words are swallowed up.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 6:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:6:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:6:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "For the arrows of the Almighty are within me, the poison whereof drinketh up my spirit: the terrors of God do set themselves in array against me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 6:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:6:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:6:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Doth the wild ass bray when he hath grass? or loweth the ox over his fodder?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 6:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:6:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:6:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Can that which is unsavoury be eaten without salt? or is there any taste in the white of an egg?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 6:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:6:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:6:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "The things that my soul refused to touch are as my sorrowful meat.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 6:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:6:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:6:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Oh that I might have my request; and that God would grant me the thing that I long for!",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 6:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:6:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:6:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Even that it would please God to destroy me; that he would let loose his hand, and cut me off!",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 6:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:6:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:6:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Then should I yet have comfort; yea, I would harden myself in sorrow: let him not spare; for I have not concealed the words of the Holy One.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 6:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:6:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:6:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "What is my strength, that I should hope? and what is mine end, that I should prolong my life?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 6:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:6:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:6:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Is my strength the strength of stones? or is my flesh of brass?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 6:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:6:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:6:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Is not my help in me? and is wisdom driven quite from me?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 6:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:6:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:6:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "To him that is afflicted pity should be shewed from his friend; but he forsaketh the fear of the Almighty.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 6:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:6:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:6:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "My brethren have dealt deceitfully as a brook, and as the stream of brooks they pass away;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 6:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:6:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:6:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "Which are blackish by reason of the ice, and wherein the snow is hid:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 6:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:6:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:6:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "What time they wax warm, they vanish: when it is hot, they are consumed out of their place.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 6:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:6:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:6:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "The paths of their way are turned aside; they go to nothing, and perish.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 6:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:6:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:6:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "The troops of Tema looked, the companies of Sheba waited for them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 6:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:6:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:6:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "They were confounded because they had hoped; they came thither, and were ashamed.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 6:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:6:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:6:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "For now ye are nothing; ye see my casting down, and are afraid.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 6:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:6:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:6:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "Did I say, Bring unto me? or, Give a reward for me of your substance?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 6:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:6:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:6:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "Or, Deliver me from the enemy’s hand? or, Redeem me from the hand of the mighty?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 6:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:6:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:6:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "Teach me, and I will hold my tongue: and cause me to understand wherein I have erred.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 6:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:6:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:6:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "How forcible are right words! but what doth your arguing reprove?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 6:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:6:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:6:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "Do ye imagine to reprove words, and the speeches of one that is desperate, which are as wind?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 6:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:6:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:6:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "Yea, ye overwhelm the fatherless, and ye dig a pit for your friend.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 6:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:6:27"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-028",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 28,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:6:28",
      "numberLabel": "28",
      "text": "Now therefore be content, look upon me; for it is evident unto you if I lie.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 6:28",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:6:28"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-029",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 29,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:6:29",
      "numberLabel": "29",
      "text": "Return, I pray you, let it not be iniquity; yea, return again, my righteousness is in it.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 6:29",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:6:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-030",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 30,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:6:30",
      "numberLabel": "30",
      "text": "Is there iniquity in my tongue? cannot my taste discern perverse things?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 6:30",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:6:30"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
